{"id":"granicus-68-270","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"CITY COUNCIL REGULAR","date":"2005-02-22","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://irvine.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=68&clip_id=270","minutes_url":"https://irvine.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=68&clip_id=270&doc_id=833fe2db-b976-43fe-a7d8-fa02a4e057f2","packet_url":"","clip_id":270,"view_id":68,"video_url":"https://irvine.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=68&clip_id=270","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"https://archive-video.granicus.com/irvine/irvine_489beae7d7d4ea8b64f0db7419266f60.mp4","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"CITY COUNCIL AGENDA\n  BETH KROM\n  Mayor\n  SUKHEE KANG  LARRY AGRAN\n  Mayor Pro Tempore  Councilmember\n  STEVEN CHOI  CHRISTINA SHEA\n  Councilmember  Councilmember\n\n  CITY COUNCIL REGULAR\n  MEETING\n  February 22, 2005\n  4:00 P.M.\n  City Council Chamber\n  One Civic Center Plaza\n  NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\nAt 11:00 p.m., the City Council will determine which of the remaining agenda items can be considered and acted\nupon prior to 12:00 midnight and will continue all other items on which additional time is required until a future City\nCouncil meeting. All meetings are scheduled to terminate at 12:00 midnight.\n\nADDITIONS AND DELETIONS TO THE AGENDA: Additions to the agenda are limited by California Government\nCode Section 54954.2 of the Brown Act and for those items that arise after the posting of the Agenda and must\nbe acted upon prior to the next City Council meeting.\n\nANNOUNCEMENTS/COMMITTEE REPORTS/COUNCIL COMMENTS: Announcements, Committee Reports\nand Council Comments are for the purpose of presenting brief comments or reports, are subject to California\nGovernment Code Section 54954.2 of the Brown Act and are limited to 15-minutes per meeting.\n\nCONSENT CALENDAR ITEMS: All matters listed under Consent Calendar are considered to be routine and all\nwill be enacted by one roll call vote. There will be no discussion of these items unless members of the City\nCouncil request specific items to be removed from the Consent Calendar for separate discussion. Any member of\nthe public may address the Council on items on the Consent Calendar. Public comments on any item or items on\nthe consent calendar are limited to three minutes per speaker. If you wish to speak to a particular item or items,\nplease complete a Speaker’s Form and give it to the City Clerk. (Please see information in “Request to Speak”\nsection.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENT: Any member of the public may address the City Council on items within the Council’s\nsubject matter jurisdiction but which are not listed on this agenda during public comments. However, no action\nmay be taken on matters that are not part of the posted agenda. Public comments are scheduled for 30 minutes\nand are limited to three minutes per person. If you wish to speak, please complete a Speaker’s Form and submit\nto the City Clerk.\n\fCITY COUNCIL – NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\nSPEAKER’S CARD/REQUEST TO SPEAK: If you would like to address the City Council on a scheduled agenda\nitem, please complete the speaker’s card. The card is at the table at the entrance to the Council Chamber. Please\nidentify on the card your name, address, and the item on which you would like to speak and return to the City\nClerk. The speaker’s card assists the Mayor in ensuring that all persons wishing to address the Council are\nrecognized. Your name will be called at the time the matter is heard by the Council.\n\nSTAFF REPORTS: As a general rule, staff reports or other written documentation have been prepared or\norganized with respect to each item of business listed on the agenda. Copies of these materials are on file with\nthe City Clerk and are available for public inspection and copying. If you have any questions regarding any item of\nbusiness on the agenda for this meeting, or any of the staff reports or other documentation relating to any agenda\nitem, please contact City Clerk staff at (949) 724-6205.\n\nPUBLIC HEARINGS: Public Hearings are scheduled for a time certain of 4:00 p.m. (unless noticed otherwise) or\nas soon thereafter as possible. City Council, when considering the matter scheduled for hearing, will take the\nfollowing actions: 1) Open the Public Hearing. 2) Receive staff report. 3) Accept public testimony. 4) City Council\ncomments and questions. 5) Take appropriate action. Those wishing to address the City Council during the Public\nHearing must complete a “Request to Speak” form and provide it to the City Clerk prior to the hearing. If, in the\nfuture, you wish to challenge in court any of the matters on this agenda for which a public hearing is to be\nconducted, you may be limited to raising only those issues which you (or someone else) raised orally at the public\nhearing or in written correspondence received by the City at or before the hearing. Any person seeking to\nchallenge a City Council decision made as a result of a proceeding in which by law a hearing is required to be\ngiven, evidence is required to be taken, and the discretion in the determination of facts is vested in the City\nCouncil, shall be required to commence that action 90 days following the date on which the decision becomes\nfinal as provided in Code of Civil Procedure Section 1094.6. Please refer to Code of Civil Procedure 1094.6 to\ndetermine how to calculate when a decision becomes “final.” Notice: Public Hearings listed for continuance will\nbe continued as noted and posting of this agenda serves as notice of continuation. Any matter not noted for\ncontinuance, will be posted separately.\n\nAMERICANS WITH DISABILITIES ACT: It is the intention of the City of Irvine to comply with the Americans With\nDisabilities Act (ADA) in all respects. If, as an attendee or a participant at this meeting, you will need special\nassistance beyond what is normally provided, the City of Irvine will attempt to accommodate you in every\nreasonable manner. Please contact Jeri L. Stately, City Clerk, at least 48 hours prior to the meeting to inform us\nof your particular needs and to determine if accommodation is feasible. Please advise us at the time if you will\nneed accommodations to attend or participate in meetings on a regular basis.\n\nThis agenda was prepared by the City Clerk. Regular meetings of the City Council are held on the second and\nfourth Tuesdays of each month at 4:00 p.m. However, study sessions and/or closed sessions are periodically\nheld prior to the start of the regular meeting. The City Council Agenda is posted in the Police Department and\navailable at your local library. It is also available through our FAX LIBRARY system. Simply dial (949) 724-6210\nand request document number 100 anytime after 5:00 p.m. on the Friday prior to a City Council meeting. The\nAgenda may also be accessed through the City’s web page at www.ci.irvine.ca.us\n\n  STATE OF CALIFORNIA  )\n  CITY OF IRVINE  ) SS\n  COUNTY OF ORANGE  )\n\n  I DECLARE UNDER PENALTY OF PERJURY that I am employed by the City of Irvine, in\n  the City Clerk’s Department; and that I posted this agenda in the posting book located in\n  the Public Safety Lobby of City Hall, One Civic Center Plaza.\n\n  Dated/Signed: ___________________________________________________________\n\n  ii\n\f  FINAL\n  AGENDA\n\n  IRVINE\n  CITY COUNCIL\n  REGULAR MEETING\n\n  February 22, 2005\n\n  NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\n  At 11:00 p.m., the City Council will determine which of the\n  remaining agenda items can be considered and acted upon\n  prior to 12:00 midnight and will continue all other items on\n  which additional time is required until a future City Council\n  meeting. All meetings are scheduled to terminate at 12:00\n  midnight.\n\nCALL TO ORDER  4:00 P.M.\n\nA regular meeting of the Irvine City Council will be called to order on February 22, 2005\nat 4:00 p.m., in the City Council Chamber, Irvine Civic Center, One Civic Center Plaza,\nIrvine, California, by Mayor Krom, presiding officer.\n\nROLL CALL\n\n  COUNCILMEMBER:  LARRY AGRAN\n  COUNCILMEMBER:  STEVEN CHOI\n  COUNCILMEMBER:  CHRISTINA SHEA\n  MAYOR PRO TEMPORE:  SUKHEE KANG\n  MAYOR:  BETH KROM\n\n*****************STUDY SESSION/WORKSHOPS/SCOPING SESSIONS*****************\n\nDevelopment of an Ethics Code (Submitted by CMO)\n\n  1\n\fCity Council Agenda  February 22, 2005\n\n***********************************************RECESS******************************************\n\n**************RECONVENE TO THE CITY COUNCIL MEETING - 5:00 P.M.**************\n\nPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\n\nMOMENT OF SILENCE\n\nMUSICAL PRESENTATION\n\nConcordia Choir, Concordia University, Irvine, will perform \"Caritas et Amor\"\nfollowed by \"Betelehemu\".\n\nPRESENTATIONS\n\n1) Government Finance Officers' Association (GFOA) Distinguished Budget\nPresentation Award (Submitted by CMO/Budget)\n\n2) Introduction of New and Newly Promoted Employees (Public\nSafety/Administration)\n\n3) United States Tennis Association, Heritage Park 2004 USA Team Tennis\nNational Champions - 14 & Under Division (submitted by Community\nServices/Athletics)\n\n4) Butterfly Initiative Project (Submitted by Community Services/Irvine Fine Arts\nCenter)\n\n5) Operation Photo - DVD and presentation by Councilmember Shea and Mitch\nGoldstone\n\nINTRODUCTIONS\n\n*ANNOUNCEMENTS/COMMITTEE REPORTS/COUNCIL REPORTS\n\n*ADDITIONS AND DELETIONS\n\n***********************************CONSENT CALENDAR************************************\n\n*PUBLIC COMMENTS (Limited to three (3) minutes per speaker)\n\n1.CITY COUNCIL MINUTES\n\n  1.1 APPROVAL OF CITY COUNCIL MINUTES (Submitted by City Clerk)\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  2\n\fCity Council Agenda  February 22, 2005\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the minutes of a regular meeting of the City Council\n  held on February 8, 2005.\n\n2.PROCLAMATIONS/COMMENDATIONS/RATIFICATIONS\n\n  2.1 COMMEND THE FOLLOWING:\n\n  a) Congratulating the Heritage Park Co-Ed 14 Advanced Tennis Team\n  2004 Orange County Spring League (14Adv) Champions\n  2004 Southern California Sectional Champions\n  2004 USA Team Tennis National Champions\n\n3.AGREEMENTS\n\n  3.1 COOPERATIVE AGREEMENT WITH CALTRANS FOR THE SAND\n  CANYON/I-5 IMPROVEMENT PROJECT (Submitted by Public\n  Works/Transportation Development)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Adopt a resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. - A RESOLUTION OF\n  THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING THE\n  COOPERATIVE AGREEMENT BETWEEN CALTRANS AND THE CITY\n  OF IRVINE FOR THE SAND CANYON/I-5 IMPROVEMENT PROJECT\n\n  2) Approve District Agreement No. 12-513 with Caltrans for the Sand\n  Canyon/I-5 Improvement Project. Authorize the Mayor to execute and the\n  City Clerk to attest the Agreement.\n\n4.ALLOCATION OF FUNDS\n\n  4.1 BUDGET ADJUSTMENT FOR LIGHTED CROSSWALK SAFETY\n  PROGRAM (Submitted by Public Works/Transportation Development)\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Approval of a Budget Adjustment accepting $53,100 from the State of\n  California, Office of Traffic Safety for Lighted Crosswalk Safety Program\n  and establishing a new CIP account.\n\n  2) Approval of a Budget Adjustment transferring $61,646.18 from various\n  Safety Projects to the new established CIP account.\n\n5.REPORTS\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  3\n\fCity Council Agenda  February 22, 2005\n\n  5.1 FY 2004-05 COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT MIDYEAR BUDGET\n  ADJUSTMENT (Submitted by Community Development/Administration)\n\n  ACTION:  Approve the Budget Adjustments increasing Community\n  Development Department General Fund revenues and expenditures by\n  $125,000; Building and Safety Fund revenues by $800,000; and Building\n  and Safety expenditures by $665,000.\n\n  5.2 IRVINE TRANSPORTATION CENTER 15-YEAR ANNIVERSARY\n  CAMPAIGN (Submitted by Public Works/Advanced Transportation)\n\n  ACTION:  Receive and file.\n\n6.RESOLUTIONS\n\n  6.1 WARRANT AND WIRE TRANSFER RESOLUTION (Submitted by\n  Administrative Services/Fiscal Services)\n\n  ACTION:  Adopt a Resolution entitled: RESOLUTION NO. - A\n  RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE\n  ALLOWING CERTAIN CLAIMS AND DEMANDS AND SPECIFYING THE\n  FUNDS OUT OF WHICH THE SAME ARE TO BE PAID.\n\nEND OF CONSENT CALENDAR\n\n*****************************************ORDINANCES*****************************************\n\n7.FIRST READING OF ORDINANCES\n\n  7.1 ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF IRVINE,\n  CALIFORNIA, CREATING SECTION 5-9-601 THROUGH 5-9-606 OF THE\n  IRVINE MUNICIPAL CODE, REGARDING PUBLIC SAFETY RADIO\n  SYSTEM COVERAGE (Public Safety/Administration)\n\n  ACTION:  Introduce for first reading and read by title only an ordinance\n  entitled: AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF\n  IRVINE, CALIFORNIA, CREATING SECTION 5-9-601 THROUGH 5-9-\n  606 OF THE IRVINE MUNICIPAL CODE, REGARDING PUBLIC SAFETY\n  RADIO SYSTEM COVERAGE\n\n8.SECOND READING OF ORDINANCES\n\n  8.1 GENERAL PLAN AMENDMENT AND MUNICIPAL CODE AMENDMENT\n  (NOISE ORDINANCE) - NOISE STANDARDS FORMULTI-FAMILY\n  BALCONIES (Submitted by City Clerk)\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  4\n\fCity Council Agenda  February 22, 2005\n\n  ACTION:  Adopt and read by title only an ordinance entitled:\n  ORDINANCE NO. 05-06 - AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF\n  THE CITY OF IRVINE APPROVING AMENDMENTS TO CHAPTER 2,\n  SECTION 6-8-204 (B), OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE TO AMEND\n  EXTERIOR NOISE STANDARDS FOR MULTI-FAMILY BALCONIES\n\n*************************************COUNCIL BUSINESS*************************************\n\n9.REPORTS\n\n  9.1 SCOPING SESSION FOR THREE GENERAL PLAN AMENDMENTS FOR\n  NEW RESIDENTIAL DEVELOPMENT IN THE IRVINE BUSINESS\n  COMPLEX\n\n  ACTION:\n  1) Receive staff report.\n\n  2) Council comments and questions.\n\n  9.2 FREEDOM OF SPEECH ORDINANCE (This item was agendized for\n  discussion by Councilmember Agran)\n\n*PUBLIC COMMENTS (Limited to three (3) minutes per speaker)\n\nADJOURNMENT\n\n  Adjourn to a CITY COUNCIL REGULAR meeting, March 8, 2005, 4:00 p.m., City\n  of Irvine, City Council Chamber, One Civic Center Plaza, Irvine, California.\n\n  NOTICE TO THE PUBLIC\n\n  The foregoing does constitute the final agenda.\n\n  The agenda is available through our FAX LIBRARY system. Simply dial\n  (949)724-6210 and request document number 100 anytime after 5:00\n  p.m., on the Friday prior to a City Council meeting. The agenda may also\n  be accessed through the City’s Web page at www.ci.irvine.ca.us\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  5\n\fCity Council Agenda  February 22, 2005\n\n*Please refer to Notice to the Public, Pages i & ii\n\nPrepared by the City Clerk’s Office  6","minutes_text":"��\u0011ࡱ\u001a�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000>\u0000\u0003\u0000�� \u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000m\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000o\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000����\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000l\u0000\u0000\u0000��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\u0000% \u0004\u0000\u0000�\u0012�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0004\u0000\u0000�0\u0000\u0000\u000e\u0000bjbj%�%�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 \u0004\u0016\u0000%_\u0000\u0000G�\u0001\u0000G�\u0001\u00003,\